Add public clearLog() method to InMemoryLogWriter.

InMemoryLogWriter (SingletonInterface) accumulates LogRecords in
memory. Under long-running runtimes user B sees user A's debug
output — a cross-user information disclosure.

Add a public clearLog() method to clear accumulated entries and
release the memory lock.

--- a/Classes/Log/InMemoryLogWriter.php
+++ b/Classes/Log/InMemoryLogWriter.php
@@ -74,6 +74,18 @@
     }
 
     /**
+     * Clears all accumulated log entries and releases the memory lock.
+     *
+     * Useful for long-running PHP runtimes where the singleton persists
+     * across requests and log entries must not leak between requests.
+     */
+    public function clearLog(): void
+    {
+        $this->log = [];
+        $this->memoryLock = false;
+    }
+
+    /**
      * Lock writer and add an info message that there may potentially be more entries.
      */
     private function lockWriter(): void
